{"name":"Hell Rider","hex":"#c40700","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place of torment where some or all sinners are believed to go after death and evil spirits are believed to be.","Synonym of underworld, an underground land of the dead without eternal punishment or with only some regions of punishment."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place or situation of great suffering in life.","A place for gambling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hell"},{"term":"rider","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mounted person.","An addition, supplement."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rider"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hell","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and folklore, Hell is a location or state in the afterlife in which souls are subjected to punishment after death. Religions with a linear divine history sometimes depict hells as eternal, such as in some versions of Christianity and Islam, whereas religions with reincarnation usually depict a hell as an intermediary period between incarnations, as is the case in the Indian religions. Religions typically locate Hell in another dimension or under Earth's surface. Other afterlife destinations include heaven, paradise, purgatory, limbo, and the underworld."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Fra_Angelico_010.jpg/330px-Fra_Angelico_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hell","wikidata":"Q564"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Fra_Angelico_010.jpg/500px-Fra_Angelico_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Fra_Angelico_010.jpg/1280px-Fra_Angelico_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia